@meta
id: 12-18
title: Scenario — the refund cleanup
chapter: 12
type: scenario
skills: search-slash, search-next, search-star, search-motion, search-offset, dot-repeat
par: 140
minutes: 14
vscode: two tabs, five Ctrl+F round trips, one nervous replace-all
vimrc: set hlsearch incsearch
open: order.provider.ts errors.json

@brief
The last job of the chapter, and the biggest. A hundred and thirty lines,
four fixes, and every one of them is found by naming it rather than by
looking for it.

    ORD-902  Refund tidy-up before the gateway migration.

  1. `legacyRefund` goes. The whole method, and the blank line after it,
     so that `refundPartial` sits directly below `submit`. The legacy
     gateway was switched off in March.

  2. `refundPartial` sends pounds to a service that expects pence. The
     `amount` it passes needs multiplying by 100. Only that one — the
     `refunded` value written to the database stays in pounds.

  3. The refund call in `cancel` still passes the old three-argument
     signature. It takes one argument now:

         await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

  4. `CANCELED` is spelled with two Ls everywhere else in the codebase.
     Three lines in this file spell it with one. Fix 1 takes care of the
     first; make the other two `CANCELLED`.

`errors.json` is open as a second file so you can check the codes exist.
It is already correct. Change anything in it and the check fails — and
because two files are open, `:wq` will not let you leave. `:wqa` writes
both and quits.

@keys
| `d/text` `Enter` | delete from here to the next match |
| `c/text` `Enter` | change from here to the next match |
| `/text/e` `Enter` | land on the last character of the match |
| `*` `n` | search for the word under the cursor, then keep going |
| `.` | repeat the last change |
| `^` | first non-blank character of the line |
| `:wqa` | write every open file and quit |

@hints
Work top to bottom and the whole job is one pass through the file. Each
fix starts with a search that names the thing you are about to change.
--
For the method: land on its first line, put the cursor at the first
non-blank character, and delete up to the next `public`. That takes the
method and its trailing blank line and leaves the indentation of the next
one intact.

For the pence fix, the amount you want is the one inside the
`refundPartial` call, not the one below it — so search for something that
only appears in the call.
--
For the signature, `c/)` `Enter` replaces the whole argument list in one
go; type the single argument and `Esc`.

For the two spellings, do the first with `ciw` and then use `n` and `.`
for the second — the search takes you there, the dot repeats the change.
Afterwards, `:wqa`.

@solution
One route through it, top to bottom.

    /legacyRefund<Enter>  ^  d/public<Enter>
    /amount: args.amount/e<Enter>  a * 100<Esc>
    /order.id, order.total<Enter>  c/)<Enter>order.id<Esc>
    /CANCELED<Enter>  ciwCANCELLED<Esc>  n  .
    :wqa<Enter>

Four fixes, one pass, no scrolling. Worth walking through what each line
is actually doing, because between them they are the whole chapter.

`d/public` is the chapter's central idea: an operator taking a search as
its motion. Deleting a method without counting its lines, without
selecting it, and without caring how long it is. Starting from `^` is
what keeps the next method's indentation.

`/amount: args.amount/e` shows why patterns are allowed to be long. A
short pattern would have matched the wrong `amount`; a long one is
specific, and the `/e` offset puts the cursor exactly where the new text
goes. Typing a longer search to avoid pressing `n` three times and
checking each one is usually the better trade.

`c/)` replaces a run of text whose two ends are a word and a bracket —
the shape no text object covers.

And the last one is the one that tells you the chapter landed: `n` then
`.`. The search took you to the next bad spelling and the dot repeated
the fix, so the second one cost two keystrokes. If your instinct there
was to type the search out again, or to reach for a replace-all across a
file you had not read, that is the instinct this chapter is for.

Search in VS Code is a way of looking at a file. Search in vim is a way
of moving through one and, once you attach an operator to it, a way of
editing it. Everything after this — regex in chapter 13, `:substitute` in
14, `:global` in 15 — is built on the pattern you just typed.

@start order.provider.ts
import { REFUND_APPROVAL_LIMIT } from '../../configuration/limits';
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerRepository } from '../customer/customer.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';
import { AuditProducer } from '../../events/audit.producer';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerRepository) protected customerRepository: CustomerRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
    @inject(AuditProducer) protected auditProducer: AuditProducer,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const customer = await this.customerRepository.findOne({
      where: { id: args.customerId },
    });

    if (!customer) {
      throw exception('CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId: customer.id });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: {
        customerId: args.customerId,
        total: args.total,
        status: 'PENDING',
      },
    });

    await this.auditProducer.publish({
      type: 'order.created',
      orderId: order.id,
    });

    return order;
  }

  public async submit(args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (order.total <= 0) {
      throw exception('ORDER_EMPTY');
    }

    await this.paymentService.charge(order.id, order.total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id: order.id },
      values: { status: 'SUBMITTED' },
    });
  }

  public async legacyRefund(args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    await this.paymentService.refundLegacy(order.id, order.total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id: order.id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELED' },
    });
  }

  public async refundPartial(args: { id: string; amount: number }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (args.amount > order.total) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refundPartial({
      orderId: order.id,
      amount: args.amount,
    });

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id: order.id },
      values: { refunded: args.amount },
    });
  }

  public async requiresApproval(args: { id: string; amount: number }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (args.amount > REFUND_APPROVAL_LIMIT) {
      return true;
    }

    return order.total > REFUND_APPROVAL_LIMIT;
  }

  public async expire(args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SUBMITTED');
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id: order.id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELED' },
    });
  }

  public async cancel(args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id, order.total, 'LEGACY');

    await this.emailService.sendCancellation(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id: order.id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { REFUND_APPROVAL_LIMIT } from '../../configuration/limits';
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerRepository } from '../customer/customer.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';
import { AuditProducer } from '../../events/audit.producer';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerRepository) protected customerRepository: CustomerRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
    @inject(AuditProducer) protected auditProducer: AuditProducer,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id: args.id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const customer = await this.customerRepository.findOne({
      where: { id: args.customerId },
    });

    if (!customer) {
      throw exception('CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId: customer.id });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: {
        customerId: args.customerId,
        total: args.total,
        status: 'PENDING',
      },
    });

    await this.auditProducer.publish({
      type: 'order.created',
      orderId: order.id,
    });

    return order;
  }

  public async submit(args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (order.total <= 0) {
      throw exception('ORDER_EMPTY');
    }

    await this.paymentService.charge(order.id, order.total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id: order.id },
      values: { status: 'SUBMITTED' },
    });
  }

  public async refundPartial(args: { id: string; amount: number }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (args.amount > order.total) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refundPartial({
      orderId: order.id,
      amount: args.amount * 100,
    });

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id: order.id },
      values: { refunded: args.amount },
    });
  }

  public async requiresApproval(args: { id: string; amount: number }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (args.amount > REFUND_APPROVAL_LIMIT) {
      return true;
    }

    return order.total > REFUND_APPROVAL_LIMIT;
  }

  public async expire(args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SUBMITTED');
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id: order.id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async cancel(args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.findOne({ id: args.id });

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    await this.emailService.sendCancellation(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id: order.id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start errors.json
{
  "ORDER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_EMPTY": { "statusCode": 422, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SUBMITTED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL": { "statusCode": 422, "sentry": false },
  "REFUND_NOT_AUTHORISED": { "statusCode": 403, "sentry": false },
  "PAYMENT_REFUND_FAILED": { "statusCode": 502, "sentry": true }
}
